1
00:00:00,059 --> 00:00:03,779
The current self-hosted quick start
describes a single Linux-server

2
00:00:03,779 --> 00:00:05,940
evaluation using Docker Compose.

3
00:00:06,320 --> 00:00:09,720
Plan separate web, API, and events
hostnames.

4
00:00:10,140 --> 00:00:13,000
Infrastructure operation is a separate
learning path from

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:14,420
department administration.

6
00:00:15,049 --> 00:00:19,490
Review the supported installer, generate
deployment-specific credentials, and

7
00:00:19,490 --> 00:00:21,520
inspect the resulting configuration.

8
00:00:21,899 --> 00:00:27,159
Start the stack, review worker migration
progress, and verify all three endpoints.

9
00:00:27,530 --> 00:00:30,659
Create the first account and department
after initialization.

10
00:00:31,409 --> 00:00:34,389
Department screens configure operational
behavior.

11
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:38,220
In this checkout, host configuration uses
public static

12
00:00:38,220 --> 00:00:40,220
fields in configuration classes.

13
00:00:40,579 --> 00:00:44,159
The configuration processor reads JSON
keys or environment

14
00:00:44,159 --> 00:00:46,159
variables and assigns those fields.

15
00:00:46,560 --> 00:00:51,800
Use the source and release documentation
to identify the exact host setting; avoid

16
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:54,160
applying a generic appsettings recipe.

17
00:00:54,760 --> 00:00:58,079
Before updating, back up the data and
configuration and

18
00:00:58,079 --> 00:01:00,079
retain prior image references.

19
00:01:00,449 --> 00:01:04,409
A rollback can require restoring the
database as well as the application.

20
00:01:04,789 --> 00:01:09,730
Treat a running evaluation as the start of
operations preparation, with monitoring

21
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:11,619
and a tested recovery procedure.

22
00:01:12,419 --> 00:01:15,850
Detailed infrastructure capture needs the
chosen deployment layout:

23
00:01:16,310 --> 00:01:21,700
Linux Compose, Windows, Kubernetes or k3s,
or an Incident Command Kit.

24
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:26,639
Record the supported release and verify
installation, endpoint connectivity,

25
00:01:26,899 --> 00:01:29,210
backup, and recovery in that environment.

26
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:32,230
Use the linked official guides for the
matching layout.

